+previous type, plus either a seed-selected leaf or, in the final growth band, a
+second fresh copy of the previous type. While each rule is assembled, its size,
+height and (a,b) state are composed from already certified child types. Thus the
+answer is known by composition of identities; generation never solves a finished
+instance. The final duplicated root branches put the root at the centre of a
+diameter and satisfy Algorithm 1's radius condition.
