   381	
   382	\noindent\textbf{Proof of the Claim:} Suppose that there exists a monochromatic color 1 path going through some
   383	two entries of $I_j$. Then the third entry should be colored with 2. There exists a monochromatic color 1 path
   384	and a monochromatic color 2 path between vertices $s_0$ and $u_{j,0}$, since any path between $s_0$ and $u_{j,3}$ goes
   385	through the vertex $u_{j,0}$. Similarly, there exists a monochromatic color 1 path and a monochromatic color 2 path between
