   390	Notice that $t_{i,7}t_{i,6}t_{i,8}$ is the only path between vertices $t_{i,7}$ and $t_{i,8}$ (see Figure \ref{cfc2}).
   391	Then we can assume that the edge $t_{i,7}t_{i,6}$ is colored with 1 and the edge $t_{i,8}t_{i,6}$ is colored with 2.
   392	We have that there exists a monochromatic color 1 path and a monochromatic color 2 path between vertices $s_0$ and $t_{i,6}$.
   393	Then the two edges $t_{i,0}t_{i,1}$ and $t_{i,0}t_{i,2}$ are colored with distinct colors by our Claim.
