The proof gives a compact, theorem-backed certificate route: a satisfying NAE assignment determines the two-color proper-path coloring in Theorem 2.1. I’m using that paper-licensed reduction, but I’ll label it representational rather than native graph coverage because the actual search is NAE-SAT. The promising Track B construction hides a full-rank cyclic XOR system inside valid NAE-3SAT clauses; generic elimination remains mechanical, while recognizing the overlap cycle gives a sub-300-operation recurrence and keeps the answer to 59 bits.
